Here's a guide to implementing OTA firmware updates on an ESP32:

## OTA Update Approaches

### 1. **Native ESP-IDF OTA** (Recommended for production)

Use the built-in `esp_https_ota` component:

```cpp
#include "esp_ota_ops.h"
#include "esp_https_ota.h"

esp_err_t perform_ota(const char *url) {
    esp_http_client_config_t config = {
        .url = url,
        .cert_pem = server_cert_pem,  // TLS cert for secure updates
    };

    esp_https_ota_config_t ota_config = {
        .http_config = &config,
    };

    return esp_https_ota(&ota_config);  // Downloads, writes, validates
}
```

### 2. **Arduino OTA** (Good for development)

```cpp
#include <ArduinoOTA.h>

void setup() {
    WiFi.begin(ssid, password);
    ArduinoOTA.setHostname("my-esp32");
    ArduinoOTA.setPassword("ota-password");
    ArduinoOTA.begin();
}

void loop() {
    ArduinoOTA.handle();
}
```

## Key Design Considerations

| Concern | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| **Partition scheme** | Use dual OTA partitions (`ota_0`, `ota_1`) so the device can roll back on failure |
| **Security** | Always use HTTPS + signature verification (`CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_ON_UPDATE`) |
| **Rollback** | Call `esp_ota_mark_app_valid_cancel_rollback()` after confirming the new firmware works |
| **Progress tracking** | Use `esp_https_ota_begin()` + `esp_https_ota_perform()` loop for progress callbacks |
| **Version checking** | Compare firmware versions before downloading to avoid unnecessary updates |

## Partition Table for OTA

```csv
# Name,   Type, SubType, Offset,  Size
nvs,      data, nvs,     0x9000,  0x4000
otadata,  data, ota,     0xd000,  0x2000
ota_0,    app,  ota_0,   0x10000, 0x1E0000
ota_1,    app,  ota_1,   0x1F0000,0x1E0000
```

## Robust OTA Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Check for update"] --> B{"New version available?"}
    B -- No --> C["Sleep / retry later"]
    B -- Yes --> D["Download to inactive OTA slot"]
    D --> E{"Verify signature & checksum"}
    E -- Fail --> F["Abort, keep current firmware"]
    E -- Pass --> G["Set boot partition to new slot"]
    G --> H["Reboot"]
    H --> I{"App self-test passes?"}
    I -- Yes --> J["Mark valid, cancel rollback"]
    I -- No --> K["Automatic rollback to previous slot"]
```

## Tips

- **Test rollback** by intentionally flashing a broken image — confirm the device recovers
- **Rate-limit retries** with exponential backoff to avoid hammering your update server
- **Store OTA URL in NVS** so it can be changed without reflashing
- Use `esp_ota_get_running_partition()` to log which slot is active

